Fetched when building, not vendored here
----------------------------------------

This source release does not distribute `esp_audio_codec` or frogfs, and
it does not distribute a firmware binary. Dependency pins are not a
firmware-binary release. Obligations below apply when someone later builds
and distributes an image that contains those object codes. Nothing in this
NOTICE clears that later distribution.

ESP-IDF component pins are in
voxmind-source-available/snapshot/firmware/dependencies.lock.
managed_components/ is not included. Notable obligations:

- espressif/esp_audio_codec (lock pin 2.6.2), declared by
  firmware/components/codec_opus/idf_component.yml.
  The component comment in this tree states that Espressif ships a
  prebuilt Opus encoder whose license allows use only with Espressif chips.
  ESP32-S3 is an Espressif chip. Do not treat that comment as permission to
  ship the codec with a non-Espressif product. The codec binary is not in
  this repository. The comment was not re-checked against a downloaded
  license file. A firmware image that links that prebuilt library is a
  distribution of the library. This source tree does not perform or
  approve that distribution.

- lvgl/lvgl (locked with espressif/esp_lvgl_port). LVGL is generally under
  its own MIT-style terms, and current LVGL 9 sources include frogfs under
  the Mozilla Public License 2.0. This repository does not vendor frogfs.
  Distributing a firmware binary that contains frogfs object code can
  trigger MPL-2.0 source obligations for those MPL files. That does not
  relicense the original VoxMind firmware. This tree does not include the
  MPL source bundle, because no firmware image was built. Shipping a
  binary later is not already satisfied by this source release.

- espressif/esp-sr, esp_modem, esp-dl and their dependencies are downloaded
  from the Espressif component registry. Their notices travel with those
  downloads. This import did not copy them and did not re-check every
  nested license beyond the pins and the component manifests in tree.

- Node dependencies listed in
  voxmind-source-available/snapshot/cloud/package.json
  (Fastify, React, the Lark/Feishu Node SDK, and others) stay under their
  own licenses. node_modules/ is not part of this release.

Unresolved combinations
-----------------------

See docs/COMPLIANCE.md. These remain open:

- A firmware binary is not part of this release. Distributing one would
  be a new distribution of `esp_audio_codec` and, if linked, of frogfs.
  That distribution is not cleared here.
- The Chinese UI font bitmaps in this tree are the regenerated Noto Sans
  SC 2.004 outputs. See fonts/README.md. A firmware image that embeds
  them is still the separate binary distribution described above.
